---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---
<Layout title="Privacy policy">
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl pb-12">
    <header>
      <p class="eyebrow">Your data</p>
      <h1 class="page-title mt-2">Privacy policy</h1>
      <p class="page-intro mt-4">Kalorec uses GitHub to sign you in and to store your recipes in repositories you choose.</p>
      <p class="muted mt-3 text-sm">Last updated September 28, 2026</p>
    </header>

    <div class="mt-10 space-y-8 leading-relaxed">
      <section aria-labelledby="account-data">
        <h2 id="account-data" class="section-title">GitHub account and login</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">When you sign in, GitHub gives Kalorec your username, numeric account ID, and an access token with repository permissions. Kalorec uses the token to access the repositories you select. Your username, token, and repository selections are kept in an encrypted, HTTP-only session cookie that expires after 30 days. Logging out removes that cookie from your browser.</p>
        <p class="mt-3">Kalorec keeps your numeric GitHub account ID to count how many distinct people have signed in. The footer displays only the total. Logging out does not remove your account ID from this count.</p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="recipe-data">
        <h2 id="recipe-data" class="section-title">Recipes and sharing</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">Recipes, images, and saved shopping lists are written to your selected private GitHub repository. If you choose to publish a recipe, Kalorec writes a copy to your selected public repository, where anyone can view it. Removing a public copy does not erase Git history, forks, caches, or copies others made while it was public.</p>
        <p class="mt-3">If you select a public sharing repository, Kalorec lists your GitHub username, selected public repository, and profile link in its <a class="text-link" href="/users">people directory</a>. Anyone can browse that directory.</p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="outside-services">
        <h2 id="outside-services" class="section-title">Other services</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">Kalorec runs on Netlify and uses GitHub for sign-in and repository storage. If you import a recipe from a URL, Kalorec requests that page from its website to read recipe details. Those services may process request information under their own privacy policies.</p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="your-choices">
        <h2 id="your-choices" class="section-title">Your choices</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">You can log out, remove recipes from your repositories, and revoke Kalorec’s access in your GitHub account settings. To ask about the login count or your account ID, contact the <a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/rkalajian">Kalorec operator on GitHub</a>. Do not include private account details in a public message.</p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
